Alice Fanart License v1.0
Copyright (c) 2026 Miyang Technology (Shanghai) Co., Ltd. ("Licensor"). All rights not expressly granted are reserved.
Contact / commercial licensing: connect@miyang.ai

1. Scope. This license covers everything in this repository: the character assets (Alice / "白艾莉", "洛小山" / Luo Xiaoshan, the fictional friends in refs/alice_friends, reference sheets, wardrobe, artwork, prompt archives), the Miyang logo, documentation, and code. Using, copying, modifying or distributing any part means you accept this license.

2. What you may do. For non-commercial purposes only, you get a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable license to: study the content; create and non-commercially share fan works based on the character assets; redistribute the repository with this license attached; run and modify the code for your own non-commercial projects.

3. Conditions. (a) When you publish a fan work, state clearly: "Alice / Luo Xiaoshan are characters of Miyang Technology (Shanghai) Co., Ltd. This is an unofficial fan work." (b) Keep this license with any redistribution. (c) Do not state or imply any partnership, endorsement or official relationship without written permission. (d) The logo may only be used to truthfully identify the source; never as your own mark, and never registered as a trademark.

4. Prohibited without prior written consent. (a) Any commercial use, including sales, paid distribution, advertising, merchandise, sticker/emoji packs (including uploading to emoji platforms), digital collectibles, paid content, monetization via sponsorship or tips, and training/fine-tuning models to replicate the characters for commercial purposes. (b) Malicious adaptation: disparaging, defaming or insulting the characters or the Licensor, or harming their reputation, including pornographic, vulgar, nude or sexually suggestive content (Alice must always be fully and appropriately dressed); violent, gory, horror, gambling or drug content; hateful, discriminatory, politically sensitive or unlawful content; speaking in the characters' name to spread false information, or using them for fraud, false advertising or attacks. (c) Impersonating the Licensor or its official accounts; registering trademarks, domains, accounts or shop names containing "Alice", "白艾莉", "洛小山" or "米羊" to mislead the public; applying for any trademark, copyright registration or other right over the character assets. (d) Transferring, renting or sublicensing the character assets, or claiming any right in them. (e) Infringing any third party's rights.

5. Ownership. All rights in the character assets (copyright, trademark, etc.) belong to the Licensor. Original parts you create yourself in a fan work belong to you, but the character likeness, names and anything derived from the character assets remain the Licensor's.

6. Breach and liability. Any breach automatically terminates your license; you must stop using the assets and remove the related works. For malicious adaptation, impersonation and commercial use, the Licensor reserves the right to pursue legal liability, including injunction, remedial measures, public apology, compensation for all losses (including reasonable enforcement costs such as notarization and attorney fees), platform takedown complaints, and litigation or arbitration. If the Licensor suffers third-party claims, proceedings, penalties or platform actions because of your fan works or breach, you bear all resulting liability and costs. This section survives termination.

7. Disclaimer. The repository is provided "as is" without warranty of any kind; to the maximum extent permitted by law the Licensor is not liable for any loss arising from your use.

8. Misc. The Licensor may publish new versions; a new version applies to content obtained after its release, and the Licensor may terminate your license for malicious use by written notice at any time. This license is governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China; disputes shall first be negotiated and, failing that, submitted to the competent people's court at the Licensor's domicile. If any provision is held invalid, the rest remains effective.
